From: Matthew Feickert <matthew.feickert@wisc.edu>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 19:00:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Keep PyNE exception messages alive after what() returns

The what() methods of FileNotFound, FileNotHDF5, GroupNotFound,
PathNotFound, NotANuclide, IndeterminateNuclideForm, NotAReaction, and
IndeterminateReactionForm built their message in a local std::string
and returned its c_str(), a pointer to memory freed when what()
returns. Reading the message is a heap-use-after-free under
AddressSanitizer, and Clang warns about it with -Wreturn-stack-address
in every translation unit that includes pyne.h. Build the message in a
member from every constructor instead, so it lives as long as the
exception object, as std::exception::what() requires. This follows
upstream pyne, which fixed NotANuclide and NotAReaction the same way
with setNaNEstr() and setNarxstr().

---
 src/pyne.h |  149 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++----------------
 1 file changed, 109 insertions(+), 40 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/pyne.h b/src/pyne.h
index c058868..94edf6c 100644
--- a/src/pyne.h
+++ b/src/pyne.h
@@ -220,7 +220,7 @@ namespace pyne {
   public:
 
     /// default constructor
-    FileNotFound () {};
+    FileNotFound () { setFNFstr(); };
 
     /// default destructor
     ~FileNotFound () throw () {};
@@ -229,19 +229,25 @@ namespace pyne {
     FileNotFound(std::string fname)
     {
       filename = fname;
+      setFNFstr();
     };
 
-    /// Creates a helpful error message.
-    virtual const char* what() const throw()
+    /// Builds the message returned by what().
+    void setFNFstr()
     {
-      std::string FNFstr ("File not found: ");
+      FNFstr = "File not found: ";
       if (!filename.empty())
         FNFstr += filename;
+    };
 
-      return (const char *) FNFstr.c_str();
+    /// Creates a helpful error message.
+    virtual const char* what() const throw()
+    {
+      return FNFstr.c_str();
     };
 
   private:
+    std::string FNFstr; ///< message returned by what()
     std::string filename; ///< unfindable filename.
   };
 
@@ -372,7 +378,7 @@ namespace h5wrap
   public:
 
     /// default constructor
-    FileNotHDF5(){};
+    FileNotHDF5(){ setFNH5str(); };
 
